Subject: [PATCH] fix: give EditBox text the client's font, insets and left
 justification

A SearchBoxTemplate box drew its text yellow, centred and against its left
edge; the client draws it white, at the left, 16 px in.

- An EditBox's <FontString> element (InputBoxVisualTemplate:
  <FontString inherits="ChatFontNormal"/>) was parsed but never applied,
  so the box had no font object. It now sets the box's font object, and
  the justification and colour the element names.
- A new EditBox justifies its text LEFT, as GetJustifyH() reports in the
  client, where a FontString starts at CENTER; the element's font object
  leaves that unless it names justifyH itself.
- <TextInsets> came only from the frame's own XML. They now come from its
  template chain as well, also for CreateFrame with a template.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
